// Global geographic AOR directory — imported verbatim from "Global_Country_Territory_AOR_Directory_2026_Corrected.xlsx".
//
// 285 geographic records (worksheet "World AOR Roster": 246 ISO 3166-1 entries, 23 additional GENC / constituent entries and
// 16 constituent segments of three split ISO parents) plus the 16-row "ISO Split Crosswalk". The values below are the workbook's own
// text: the workbook's evidence label, source date text and notes are PROVENANCE and are never edited here. Normalization to
// internal command ids, evidence classes and controlling-source corrections happens in global-directory.ts, so the original
// claim and the corrected claim can both be shown.
//
// Workbook rules (sheet "Read Me"): one primary AOR per location; the grouped ISO labels US, UM and TF are broken out by
// constituent geography; disputed sovereignty is not multiple AORs; some rows are regional geographic mappings rather than
// expressly named official assignments; a geographic AOR does not establish operational control.

